  message: "Filed while landing PR #227. Sibling of INV-linub (class), INV-fokik and INV-fazim - all four came out of the same nine-language catalogue-reach measurement, ~/hypergumbo_lab_notebook/taint-area-08052026/INV-linub-CHAIN-MEASUREMENT.md. This one is the only PRE-EXISTING member: PR #227 did not create it, it only made it visible by adding the kwarg and using it on one branch."  # 0dd7
- op: discuss  # 563b
  at: '2026-08-25T04:13:58Z'  # 563b
  by: agent  # 563b
  actor: jgstern_agent  # 563b
  clock: 4  # 563b
  nonce: 563b  # 563b
  message: "PHASE 0 RE-VERIFICATION AT TIP, 2026-08-25, dev e41a655d6d. Probe + fixtures:\n~/hypergumbo_lab_notebook/campaign_p0_08252026/ (probe_recv.py, rx/).\n\nTHE TITLE IS REFUTED. THE STATEMENT IS NOT — and the defect is WIDER than\nthis item says. WI-sajis (PR #498) stamped call_construct on the\nunresolved-external method path, so \"java sets call_construct on NO\nunresolved edge\" is no longer true. What survives is every receiver that is\nnot a bare identifier. Measured, control in the same run:\n\n  java   f.mkdirs()                 cc=method     <- CONTROL\n         new File(\"/x\").mkdirs()    cc=ABSENT   name=mkdirs\n         get().mkdirs()             cc=ABSENT   name=mkdirs\n         ((File) o).mkdirs()        cc=ABSENT   name=mkdirs\n         f.getParentFile().mkdirs() cc=ABSENT   name=mkdirs\n  scala  f.createNewFile()          cc=method     <- CONTROL\n         new File(..) / get() / asInstanceOf  cc=ABSENT\n  swift  fm.createFile(...)         cc=method     <- CONTROL\n         get() / (o as! FileManager)          cc=ABSENT\n  objc   every message-send shape   cc=method     <- clean\n  rust   f.sync_all(), get().sync_all()  cc=method <- clean\n\nMECHANISM, one predicate per analyzer. java.py:1964 derives the stamp from\nreceiver_name being a bare identifier:\n    pr4_call_construct = \"method\" if receiver_name and receiver_name != \"this\" else None\nso a receiver EXPRESSION reads as \"no receiver at all\". scala and swift have\nthe same shape. This item names only java; the defect is java + scala + swift.\n\nWHY WI-sajis' PARITY GATE DID NOT CATCH IT. Its fixtures use plain\nreceiver.method(). That is the one-arm-of-the-wrong-arm shape sajis itself\ncorrected for cast receivers in scala/swift -- generalised: it is ALL complex\nreceivers, in three languages, not casts in two.\n\nTHE FAIL-OPEN DIRECTION, confirmed by reading the consumer.\n_register_sanitizer_callers (taint.py:2063) refuses an unresolved bare-name\nsanitizer match ONLY when call_construct == \"method\". With the key absent the\nedge reaches the permit branch and registers a PHANTOM BARRIER; since PR #214\na barrier earns sanitized and a sanitized flow is DROPPED from the claim's\nviolation set. So the missing stamp deletes findings. That is why this item is\na Phase-1 (fail-open) member and its recall-side siblings (INV-gijis /\nINV-tanom / INV-suril) are not.\n\nSTATUS UNCHANGED: violated. Not stale."  # 563b
